          TIP("Never compare velocity between teams or use it as a performance target. Story points are relative to each team, so targets simply inflate the estimates. See our guide to [Scrum velocity](/project-management/scrum/scrum-velocity/)."),
          H3("Worked example: reading the signals (illustrative)"),
          "Over four sprints, a team's throughput rises from 14 to 19 items per sprint, which looks positive. But escaped defects rise from 2 to 7 per sprint and the health check shows people working late before every review. Instead of praising the speed, the manager brings the three trends to the team's monthly review. The team decides to strengthen its [Definition of Done](/project-management/agile/definition-of-done/) with automated tests and to cap work in progress. Two sprints later throughput settles at 16, defects fall to 3 and late working stops. The balanced view prevented a short-term gain from hiding a long-term cost.",
